      "usage": {
        "purpose": "Resolve a specific evidence gap with the responsible original analyst so any downstream reviewer can revise its judgment.",
        "inputs": "Only analyst and question. The host supplies the trusted original research context, configured analyst model and frozen capability selection; do not pass workflow IDs, credentials or reconstructed prompts.",
        "outputs": "Accepted Run: use host_runs_wait/read. Completed run.output contains {from,to,question,markdown,run_ref,source_refs}. Read the complete answer before relying on it. Further material questions may call again; completed answers reach later roles and the final result, including answers requested by the manager.",
        "prerequisites": [
          "Caller must be a bull, bear, risk or manager member of investment_research_analyze; report-only rewriting does not acquire new evidence.",
          "The originally selected model and source/method capabilities remain configured at their frozen revisions."
        ],
        "limitations": [
          "No fixed round count. Ask only when further evidence or clarification can materially change the judgment; unresolved differences are valid results.",
          "Only one original analyst is assigned per call. Independent questions may be asked separately; each answer remains on the same analyst node.",
          "Does not wake a completed Run, start a new team, widen source permissions, publish reports or perform trading. A follow-up is a new native Agent Run bound to the original member.",
          "Access restrictions and missing evidence are reported honestly. A question is not proof that its proposed causal explanation is true.",
          "When a missing fact materially limits the judgment, use an existing verification outcome or a concrete capability/coverage limit to explain the boundary. If applicable analyst capabilities remain and no check was attempted, ask a targeted question; an inherited unknown is not proof of unavailability. Do not repeat failed acquisition without a new path or pursue nonessential completeness."
        ]
      },
      "binding": {
        "type": "native",
        "name": "investment_research_ask"
      }
    }
